# LOOP O (R33) — the continuation licence's two verdicts asserted over ONE pair.
# tab:continuesTable says "one logical table, cut by the page edge"; tab:licenceRefused says
# "two independent tables that merely share a template". Both is not a richer record, it is a
# contradiction: every consumer of a chain would be free to pick the reading it liked.
@prefix tab: <https://w3id.org/iladub/tab#> .
@prefix ex:  <https://example.org/tab-demo#> .
ex:p0table a tab:Table .
ex:p1table a tab:Table ;
    tab:continuesTable ex:p0table ;
    tab:licenceRefused ex:p0table .
